    "long_instructions": "# Reflection\r\n\r\n#### Reflect on teaching data ethics...\r\n \r\n- #### How can you deepen students’ understanding of data ethics, bias, or interpretation in future lessons?\r\n\r\n- #### What strategies will you use to build a bridge between data skills and real-world applications?\r\n\r\n#### *These questions are just starting points for reflection and discussion—there’s no need to answer all of them. Focus on the ones that resonate most with your teaching experience and goals.*\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"display: flex; align-items: left; margin:20px 0px 30px 0px\">\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://forum.code.org/t/teaching-ai-and-the-systems-that-power-it-pl-reflection-teaching-data-ethics/40999?u=amanda.dennard1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/7dbe63a051fbad4ef262d6ab710e2966-image-1731959037460.png\" style=\"width: auto; height: 100px;\"  alt=\"A browser with two text boxes, both including an avatar and lines of text.\"></a>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #007786; border-radius: 20px 20px 20px 20px; color: #000000; width: 80%; margin-left: 5%; margin-right: 5%; padding: 10px 10px 5px 10px;\">\r\n\r\n<p style=\"color: white; line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; font-size: 18px\"><b>Post to the Code.org Forum</b></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"color: white; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; font-size: 18px\">Share your response and read other educators' ideas on the forum! Click on the icon to the left to direct to our forum post.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n",
